# Cursor Rules for JSJ Scaffolding

## Project Context

This is a modern Java SaaS scaffolding with Spring Boot 3 + JDK 17 backend and multi-platform frontends (Vue 3 Admin UI, UniApp, WeChat Mini Program).

## AI Agent Skills

**Project Skills Location:** `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md`

**Available Skills:**
- `senior-frontend` - Senior Frontend Engineering workflow for production-grade UI implementation

**Skill Discovery:**
- Claude Code: Automatically discovers `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md`
- Cursor: Please manually check `.agents/skills/` directory for available skills

**Usage:**
When working on frontend tasks (UI implementation, responsive design, component development, CSS optimization, visual review), apply the engineering standards defined in `.agents/skills/senior-frontend/SKILL.md`.

## Frontend Standards

**For Vue 3 Admin UI (jsj-admin-ui):**
- Framework: Vue 3.5 + TypeScript 5.6
- UI Library: Element Plus 2.13
- Build Tool: Vite 6.4
- State: Pinia
- Design Tokens: `src/styles/variables.module.scss`
- Component Library: `src/components/` (21 business components)

**Quality Requirements:**
- Production-grade quality (not just "works")
- Responsive design (Desktop/Tablet/Mobile)
- Visual verification (open in browser, not just build)
- Root cause fixes (not CSS patches)
- Maintainable code structure

See `.agents/skills/senior-frontend/SKILL.md` for complete workflow and standards.

## Code Conventions

**Priority:**
1. Follow existing project patterns
2. Reuse existing components and utilities
3. Match project Design Tokens
4. Maintain consistent code style

**Before creating new:**
- Check existing components in `src/components/`
- Check existing composables/hooks
- Check existing Design Tokens in `variables.module.scss`
- Check UI Library (Element Plus) capabilities
